{"id":1155,"level":74,"name":"Форсування загрозою мату","group":"Форсовані ходи","format":27,"description":"<p>If a chess player overlooks a mate threat, it&rsquo;s game over. That&rsquo;s why mate threats make strong forcing moves. Very often, the only way to defend against a mate threat is by giving up material.<br /><br />In the example, Black can win the white rook by first threatening mate with his own king.<br /><br />Mate threats are less forcing than checks. Your opponent might decide to react with a counterattack against your king. Always be aware of that possibility.<br /><br /><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />Win material by a mate threat.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":74,"examples":[{"fen":"8/8/8/3P4/1P2Pp2/4kP2/7r/2RK4 b - - 0 1","pgn":"1... Kd3 2. Ke1 Rh1+ 3. Kf2 Rxc1 1-0","text":"<p>Погрожуючи матом <strong>1...Kd3</strong>, білий король потрапляє в біду. Потім виграємо туру шпажкою.</p>","format":27}],"puzzles":[{"id":40236,"fen":"rnbq1rk1/p3bppp/1p2pn2/3pN1BQ/3P4/2NBP3/PP3PPP/R3K2R w - - 0 1","pgn":"1. Bxf6 Bxf6 (1... h6 +-) 2. Qxh7# 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":51163,"fen":"5rk1/1p6/2p1R1p1/8/2P5/4Q2P/Pq3Pp1/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rg8]} 1. Rxg6+ {[%csl Rg8]} (1. Qg3?  ) (1. Kxg2?  ) 1... Qg7 (1... Kh7 2. Qh6#) 2. Rxg7+ (2. Qe6+ Kh7 3. Rxg7+ (3. Rg4?  ) (3. Rg3?  )) (2. Rxg2?  ) ( 2. Qh6) 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":40241,"fen":"7k/p4p2/1p2b2p/4P3/4N3/6R1/r5PP/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"1. Nf6 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":40248,"fen":"6k1/5ppb/1b5p/pppP4/5P2/PPB2QPP/7K/4r3 b - - 0 1","pgn":"1... Be4 2. Bxe1 (2. Qf2 Rh1#) 2... Bxf3 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":45201,"fen":"4b2k/1p3q2/p3p3/P1Pp3r/3Pp3/4PpQP/1R5K/6R1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Yh8]} 1. Rxb7 ! Qxb7 (1... Qf8 2. Rg7 Bf7 3. c6) 2. Qg8# 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiTheme